      <Desc>Artist Residency Program: Relevant, contemporary visual arts practices inspire our visual arts education programs with a focus on creating spaces for expression by fostering community and connection in the classroom. Artmaking provides a conduit for igniting the creativity within each young person, helps students process and express feelings, fostering community with peers, and building self-esteem in a supportive yet challenging environment.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>339754</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>168540</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Mural Program: ArtReach believes in the power of community and art to change lives and spaces. A mural provides an opportunity for people to work together while creating something transformative and lasting for their site. The ArtReach Mural Program works directly with youth at schools and community centers to dream up large collaborative works that represent their vision.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>300258</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>116476</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Community Programs: ArtReachs Community Programs focus on providing art education to San Diego County with the guiding principles of cultivating artistic community and equitable access to art for all. Community Programs focus on craft and process-based visual arts programming for local community organizations. Our programming focuses on collaboration, investigating identity, and highlighting the practices of local professional artists.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
